<description>&lt;p&gt;Violent clashes continue between Viv Ansanm gangs and Haitian security forces, now reinforced by a Kenya-led multinational mission patrolling Port-au-Prince and Kenscoff. The Dominican army has supplied large ammunition stocks to the 400 Mawozo gang, boosting its firepower against security forces. Erik Prince is operating an anti-gang mercenary effort in Haiti, adding a private-security dimension to the conflict. The United Nations has allocated an additional US$75 million for life-saving aid to 507,000 people, and the Security Council renewed sanctions on Haiti for another year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/10/1168598&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE1PSDNZYklwbFlURFR4ZWw5TXBzM2kxUUV5SEZfZHFESFdkUVU2Q2tKUHZJSzBNeFNGZmlfTUQtb0pzaFJZNllRRjNMajF1RkJBdkNkcGF4aHVabFF4TzNteUhEQWVsazkxMnhJeFdSZVZfekluWW8xZjJSX2VYQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Trinidad Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxNZUQwWXpVMHR6Q1AxNFUwMGV5Rnc0XzhzN21LUDVWaUZQTEp3QUdtYVFIRy1FUFdJdXJTejA1V010UlBib004TEtjU1RWeXVNRHhCTmFRdndHQ1lsZzVYZEtZdXBDLUlINDVEbm1kQ2NkR05GTnB3R2toN1VJRFUtRVRFWi1XXy02d1FBRElzak5tYTFnZWJVMDBEVDMyY3ZnMXBSNW90OA?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxNYmFYUTY3LU1GZ1MzTVBCdEMtQndVRF85dC14VzhYZDJGM18yZHBUdVByeVc1cXBvUXl3QkNvMkdnamN5cml5SUN3T19Hd2gzQ3VEVXBqLTk4X25HbWFNUVVFeTZEdXExbVVwVHdjSVBLVU0zOEIyUFJkdGxJcm85QXlZeFZ3WDNTek9YeVo3bUN5bHV4cmc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Traders Union&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigwFBVV95cUxQTjc0T2pyZzY5Vk45bTlTS1k2WUhGS1U2d2h6YkpkNVNxb2ZWek9INm9UZWFUazBjT1lxZnZHYlljSWY5ZDMwTVRKVHBTdHlmTTZoY1ZHYUJ4WlVnZTAzaUtRTkJpM3Z3TmM5QWczb2tURmZobDR5QWxZVXl3bHNxSTN5bw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Mirage